- sys/types
- sys/shrine
- sys/schema
- sys/view
- sys/hand

' --- containers ---

+  uon
  '  An ordered map from iota to v, using the strict /lt_iota order.
  '  Size-balanced binary-search-tree internals (the bst.foil scheme).
  (@@ v)
  & uon/empty
    uon/node[v]
  +  empty
    :
  +  node
    :  sz=nat key=iota val=v l=uon[v] r=uon[v]
  +  kv
    '  One entry, as /uon/tap returns them.
    :  key=iota val=v

' --- shrine ---

+  track
  '  One care's local clock and its dense data-case history.  Epochs
  '  maps local data case -> sovereign commit epoch; shape is a count
  '  only and has no historical query axis.
  :  =lock epochs=uon[nat] past=row[track/leaf]
  +  leaf
    '  /track/span sealed data cases behind one pin; epochs is the
    '  open tail above them.
    :  held=pin[uon[nat]]
+  ever
  '  The three path-local care histories for one namespace path.
  '  Only explicitly asserted paths (live records or tombstones) own
  '  one.  Transparent structural spines never acquire a ledger.
  :  x=track y=track z=track
+  zeta
  '  Pattern over one path segment: a literal iota, or a typed
  '  variable constrained to an aura.
  &  zeta/lit
     zeta/var

  +  lit
    :  i=iota

  +  var
    :  aura=nat
+  soma
  '  A pattern-trie of typing requirements over a subtree: an
  '  optional lash here plus zeta-edged arms.  Matching precedence
  '  is lit over var; at most one var arm per node.
  :  fil=maybe[lash] kids=row[soma/arm]
  +  arm
    :  pat=zeta sub=soma
  +  new
    '  The empty soma: no lash here, no arms.
    ^  soma
    |  soma .none []
  +  step
    '  The sub-soma one segment selects: a lit arm on iota equality
    '  wins outright; the var arm admits only a matching aura and
    '  yields when no later lit claims the segment.
    \  seg=iota s=soma
    ^  maybe[soma]
    %  j=nat 0
       var=maybe[soma] .none
    ^  maybe[soma]
    ?  (ge j s.kids.len)  var
    =  a  s.kids.at(j)
    ?  a.pat
     > (./lit i)
       ?  (eq_iota i seg)  (./some a.sub)
       |  _ j.inc var
     > (./var tag)
       ?  (eq tag (aura_tag seg))  (_ j.inc (./some a.sub))
       |  _ j.inc var
  +  at
    '  The lash this soma assigns to a path: one /step per segment,
    '  the landing node's fil.  .none off the trie or at a lash-less
    '  node.
    \  pax=path s=soma
    ^  maybe[lash]
    %  i=nat 0
       cur=soma s
    ^  maybe[lash]
    ?  (eq i pax.len)  cur.fil
    <  sub  (soma/step pax.at(i) cur)
    |  _ i.inc sub
+  deed
  '  Options for dependency injection.
  :  req=bool
+  fief
  '  A dependency: injection options, the read restriction it
  '  needs, and the shape it requires of the target.
  :  =deed
     =care
     =soma
+  yoke
  '  A whole namespace spec: the record at the root, pattern-typed
  '  kids, and concrete-path deps.
  :  self=lash
     kids=row[soma/arm]
     deps=axal[fief]
  +  at
    '  The lash a yoke assigns to a spec-relative path: the root's
    '  own lash at [], the kid trie below.
    \  pax=path y=yoke
    ^  maybe[lash]
    ?  (eq 0 pax.len)  (./some y.self)
    |  soma/at pax (soma .none y.kids)

' --- dispatch ---

+ pails
  +  code
    '  A compiled entry riding opaquely in the namespace: the publisher's compiler
    '  mirror stores each declaration's compiled value here.  The
    '  any type is the untyped carrier (the value may be a law, row, or pin) —
    '  read it back out, never do arithmetic on it.
    :  v=any
+  move
  '  An outbound effect: one command, emitted at src, addressed
  '  outside the processed subtree.
  :  src=path dst=path w=writ
+  job
  '  What a dispatch sees: a command (the target is the flue's dst),
  '  a child-change gift, or a dependency-change notification of
  '  (care, path) pairs.
  &  job/vine
     job/take
     job/hear

  +  vine
    :  w=writ

  +  take
    :  gift=axal[mode]

  +  hear
    :  changed=row[dep]
+  flue
  '  A linearized work unit: who caused it, where it lands, what it is.
  :  src=path dst=path job=job
+  task
  '  One top-level event: a single path-tagged command, or change
  '  notifications (changed path -> its cared subscribers, as /dep
  '  pairs).
  &  task/vine
     task/vines
     task/hear

  +  vine
    :  p=path w=writ

  +  vines
    '  Several path-tagged commands in one event: admitted whole or
    '  refused whole, one journal entry.
    :  ws=row[[p=path w=writ]]

  +  hear
    :  news=axal[row[dep]]
+  fate
  '  The kernel's answer: resolved notes in /lte_pith (tap) order
  '  and outbound commands. Warp can occur only in commands, not notes.
  :  write=row[[p=path q=note]] effects=row[move]
+  worm
  '  The per-event transaction.  down is a row+cursor queue (pop at
  '  dcur, push snoc).  prize records how each path changed, for the
  '  gift cascade.
  :  toil=axal[note] down=row[flue] dcur=nat up=row[move] prize=axal[mode] now=nat eny=nat
+  eyes
  '  The watcher index: watched path -> its cared watchers, in the
  '  same dep orientation as news (p is the watcher).
  axal[row[dep]]
+  hive
  '  The crew index: what each crew-bearing node WATCHES, keyed by
  '  that node's path — /eyes turned around.  Reactions no longer keep
  '  one: the commit maintains the kernel's dependency index at
  '  /<self>/idx/deps (idx.foil), and lens translation reads only its
  '  derived keys back into this orientation.  It shares /eyes'
  '  representation deliberately: a fresh axal instantiation would be
  '  a fresh monomorphization to compile.
  axal[row[dep]]
+  lens
  '  The derived-watcher index: TRIGGER path -> lens eyes.  Each
  '  entry keeps the trigger care to test against a sign, and the
  '  watcher with its original derived dep, so the news speaks the
  '  subscriber's vocabulary (rely paths are the derived paths they
  '  named in their crew).
  axal[row[[tc=care od=dep w=path]]]

' --- store ---

+  ass
  '  An assertion: a committed version (/saga, from shrine_types),
  '  or a tombstone.  Tombstones carry their versioning too: a
  '  removal is a version like any other.  Recursive cull ensures a
  '  dead node has no live descendants; revival continues its
  '  existing locks.
  &  ass/ker
     ass/nul
     ass/past

  +  ker
    :  saga=saga

  +  nul
    :  aeon=aeon

  +  past
    ' Sealed older assertions, linked at key 0 of the open tail.
    : held=pin[uon[ass]]

+  tome
  '  One path's assertion history behind a pin: snapshots
  '  re-serialize only paths the event touched, never the rest of
  '  the index.  Same named-row necessity as /chest — and declared
  '  before its first user: value references do not resolve forward.
  :  held=pin[uon[ass]]

+  urn
  '  One path's care clocks behind a pin — the cases ledger pays
  '  per touched path, not per known path, on every snapshot.
  :  held=pin[ever]

+  chest
  '  One epoch's journaled raw diffs behind a pin: immutable once
  '  written, one content-addressed unit forever.  A named row —
  '  recursive generics need path-shaped arguments, and neither a
  '  bare pin[...] spelling nor an alias to one is.
  :  held=pin[axal[note]]

+  lchunk
  '  256 sealed epochs of journal refs behind one pin.
  :  held=pin[row[chest]]

+  ledger
  '  The append-only epoch journal: sealed chunks plus the open
  '  tail.  Write-only in the kernel; epochs address by position
  '  (1-based, matching the epoch each put committed).
  :  sealed=row[lchunk] open=row[chest]

+ reference_edge
  : holder=path slot=path target=safe

+ reference_index
  : into=axal[row[reference_edge]] past=uon[pin[axal[row[reference_edge]]]]

+  sov
  '  The versioned namespace of one czar.  rec and idx are keyed by
  '  the sovereign-wide commit epoch; top is the latest epoch and 0
  '  is reserved.  cases is a separate path-indexed ledger of local
  '  x/y/z clocks and their data-case to epoch mappings.
  '
  '  rec journals each epoch's raw diffs behind one pin: the entry
  '  is immutable once written, so snapshots re-serialize only the
  '  epoch spine, never past journals.
  '
  '  Grading, in one place.  An assertion moves its own x.  y is a
  '  frontier care: a live node absorbs its subtree's grades, a
  '  dead or transparent one lets them show through.  Every
  '  asserted ancestor's z moves.  Creations and removals grade 2;
  '  equal resolved writes are discarded before propagation.
  '  Epochs are global; every nonzero grade bumps exactly one
  '  path-local data counter, and grade 2 also bumps its
  '  independent shape counter.  Transparent paths mint nothing:
  '  no ledger, no assertion, no timestamp, no sign.
  :  rec=ledger idx=axal[tome] top=nat cases=axal[urn] references=reference_index

' --- namespace ---

+ system_publication
  : revision=nat state=sov definitions=pin[row[[path nat]]]

+ namespace_event
  ' Local audit data. This is unsigned; the system pin records the exact
  ' trusted definition set selected for this transaction.
  : system=pin[system_publication] changes=pin[axal[note]] predecessor=nat now=nat block=nat

+ namespace
  : self=iota local=sov system=pin[system_publication]
  + committed
    : state=namespace signs=axal[sign]

' --- view plans ---

+  view_select
  ' The part of a read a computation observes. Missing slots are observations
  ' too: adding a previously absent slot must invalidate a cached answer.
  & view_select/all view_select/slots view_select/names
  + all
    :
  + slots
    : keys=row[path]
  + names
    :
+  view_read
  : source=safe select=view_select
+  view_plan
  ' What a woven ctor returns: a pure computation that pauses when it
  ' needs a named input.  A graft hands the branch to a name; nothing
  ' is copied.
  & view_plan/done view_plan/need view_plan/graft view_plan/fail
  + done
    : tree=axal[myth]
  + need
    : read=view_read next={\ res[axal[myth]]}view_plan
  + graft
    : source=safe
  + fail
    : reason=str
+  woven
  ' The woven ctor: get receives the cell's own slots, the care asked
  ' for, the path beneath the cell, and what to select, and returns a
  ' plan: done with a tree; need a read, which the kernel supplies
  ' before continuing; graft onto a name, nothing copied; or fail.
  ' It reads only what it asks for, and what it read is kept beside
  ' the answer, so a cached answer can be checked without rerunning.
  : get={\ myth care path view_select}view_plan
+  view_observation
  : read=view_read value=res[axal[myth]]
+  view_evaluation
  : value=res[axal[myth]] observations=row[view_observation] steps=nat fault=str
+  view_contribution
  : source=safe value=pail
+  view_alternatives
  ' Conflicting values remain attributed alternatives, never last-writer wins.
  : values=row[view_contribution]
+  view_origins
  : sources=row[safe]

